{"Default-exported component is named TwoFactor but the file/component is for backup codes, making stack traces/React DevTools misleading": 0.7404350638389587, "Log message says 'backup code login' but endpoint is disabling 2FA, making operational logs misleading when diagnosing failures": 0.2702760696411133, "Backup codes are generated as lowercase hex but user input isn't normalized - uppercase input from password managers would be rejected even if the code is correct": 0.8654457330703735, "Backup code consumption is not atomic: two concurrent login attempts with the same backup code can both pass indexOf() before either update runs, allowing one-time code reuse": 0.9211817383766174, "resetState() doesn't clear/revoke the generated ObjectURL for the backup-codes download, causing Blob URL leaks when modal is closed/reopened multiple times": 0.6404487490653992, "Password visibility toggle button is removed from tab order via tabIndex={-1}, making it inaccessible to keyboard-only users": 0.9061102867126465, "UI always shows success toast after navigator.clipboard.writeText even though it can reject (permissions, insecure context), giving false 'copied' success for backup codes": 0.9130764603614807, "backupCodes are decrypted and JSON.parse'd without validation/handling in the login flow - if encryption key changes or data is corrupted, this throws an unhandled exception": 0.8570246696472168, "backupCodes are decrypted and JSON.parse'd without validation/handling in the disable endpoint - if encryption key changes or stored value is corrupted, JSON.parse will throw and crash the endpoint instead of returning structured error": 0.8228947520256042}